"Coyle resents a stranger at the master's bench on her first day, and watches her for slack."
"Coyle warms to anyone who works steady and asks good questions; he says little either way."
"A sorter who gauges fast and never mis-trays earns Coyle's respect inside a week."
"Nala's exact reading makes the gauge card easy; she can sort faster than any apprentice."
"Brass parts with a live glyph feel faintly strange to Nala's still flare: a prickle, then quiet."
"Tessa Voyle works at the bench nearest the sorting table, and talks to Nala before nine."
